  "current_review_test_status": "Supplied tests statically inspected only; independently authored controls, if any, are separately identified.",
  "mathematical_scope": "Vectorized radix sparse-input DFT, equivalent decomposition for valid sparse coordinates.",
  "cost_scope": "k*m<=N phase terms when1<=k<=N and power-of-two width; full N output plus width-b FFTs.",
  "test_and_evidence_limitations": "No support index/value or k<=N validation. Invalid keys can be periodic aliases, n outside range, or m=0/division errors; nonfinite values propagate. Dictionary uniqueness alone does not ensure valid coordinate domain.",
  "findings": "For valid in-range sparse maps, residue scatter, twist then length-b transforms ordered via transpose/reshape produce frequencies q+m*l. Coordinates outside0..n-1 are silently treated periodically instead of rejected; k>N yields b>N,m0 and broken shape. This fast helper has weaker input guards than main backend.",
  "source_line_evidence": [
    "15-24 n guard, missing key/value guards and phase shape",
    "25-36 scatter, twist and full output reorder"
  ],
